# AN ARCH LINUX MICROVM RUNNING KDE PLASMA BIGSCREEN ON WAYLAND, ON A virtio-gpu DISPLAY.
#
# THE DISPLAY DEVICE IS virtio-gpu OVER PCIe, so card0 carries both a Virtual-1 output and
# renderD128 - the pair KWin's DRM backend needs. See the long note in arch-rootfs.sh.
#
# THE CAPTURE IS THE SCANOUT. It is the same KWin as plasma and plasma-mobile, so the same two
# limits apply to reading it through a protocol: no wlr-screencopy (measured: `strings
# kwin_wayland` finds none) and a ScreenCast portal that stops at a consent dialog. Neither says
# anything about the pixels - virtio-gpu drives a real framebuffer, and qemu's screendump is
# what this walkthrough measures. See the plasma-mobile walk for the measurements.

walkthrough "plasma-bigscreen microvm - the TV shell on Wayland, captured from the scanout"
  resolution 1024x768
  recording_resolution 1024x768

  needs arch-vmlinuz arch-initramfs arch.qcow2
  disk arch.qcow2

  boot as a microvm from kernel "arch-vmlinuz" and initramfs "arch-initramfs" with "console=ttyS0 root=/dev/vda rw rootfstype=ext4" with a desktop with memory 1536, waiting up to 240s

  the console will say "login"
  the console will say "vmuser"

  the console will say "ARCH-SESSION-STARTING: plasma-bigscreen"

  # THE TV SHELL'S FIRST LAYOUT - the launcher grid over the wallpaper - takes longer than a
  # bare compositor to settle.
  wait 35s

  read the whole screen as "screen"

  step "the screen is not black"
    check == {name: screen_is_not_black, from: screen, mode: mean_between, rect: [0, 0, 1024, 768], rect_at: [1024, 768], range: [1, 255]}
  step "the screen is not one flat colour"
    check == {name: screen_has_content, from: screen, mode: spread_between, rect: [0, 0, 1024, 768], rect_at: [1024, 768], range: [1, 128]}

  stop the machine by killing it, waiting up to 60s
